{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Therefore she called his name Yehudah.</b> For this name contains letters of the revered Name, and together with this, the sense of thanksgiving (הודאה). And it appears that all these were names of earlier people, as we find previously Yehudit daughter of Beeri (Genesis 26:34), and likewise Shemuel son of Amihud (Numbers 34:20) before Shemuel the prophet — and they would choose from the preexisting names those that fit the expression of what had occurred."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:23.061649145Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}